# Values several stages share; Flux substitutes them as ${NAME} into the
# infrastructure-configs, platform, platform-backups and apps stages.

# The site, dashboard (/dashboard) and api (/api). Cloudflare: an A record to
# the public IP, proxied, with an Origin Rule that matches this hostname and
# overrides the destination port to 9443; SSL/TLS Full (strict) and Always
# Use HTTPS. Dynamic DNS (infrastructure/configs/cloudflare-ddns.yaml) keeps
# the address current.
PUBLIC_DOMAIN=snapflow.io
# Object storage and the image registry: A records to the public IP, DNS only
# (Cloudflare's proxy caps request bodies at 100 MB and layers are larger),
# reached on 9443 and kept current by dynamic DNS.
STORAGE_DOMAIN=storage.snapflow.io
REGISTRY_DOMAIN=registry.snapflow.io
# The sandbox zone. It must be its own registrable domain so sandbox pages are
# cross-site to the dashboard (the api refuses to start otherwise); file it
# with the Public Suffix List (private section) so each sandbox host is its
# own site. Cloudflare: an A record per edge's public host, DNS only; that host
# as the Custom Hostnames fallback origin; Authenticated Origin Pulls on. The
# api creates every sandbox CNAME with SNAPFLOW_CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, which
# needs DNS and custom hostname access to this zone.
PLATFORM_DOMAIN=snapflow.run
# The api sends from noreply@ this domain through Resend. Add it under Domains
# in Resend and copy its records into the zone, DNS only: the DKIM TXT record
# resend._domainkey.mail, the MX (priority 10) and SPF TXT records on
# send.mail, and a DMARC TXT record on _dmarc (start at p=none). Create a
# Resend API key with sending access to this domain only for RESEND_API_KEY.
EMAIL_DOMAIN=mail.snapflow.io
# Off-cluster backups (platform/backups and platform/data/postgres-backups.yaml):
# the R2 S3 endpoint of the Cloudflare account that owns the bucket.
BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=https://74bcfe44629d279b31d58f3dbd5170af.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=snapflow-backups
